{
  "_doc": "How each generic matchup parameter is applied using the kit's learned observations.\nscale: value v (0..1) placed between the learned default and the learned extreme (checkbox-like 0/1 settings turn on at v >= 0.5). span [a,b]: only that fraction of the default->extreme range is used.\nrate: for settings that count repetitions over the whole effect (Rotations, Cycles, Count). The value is a RATE per 'second', 'beat' or 'bar' (range [lo,hi], chosen by v) multiplied by the effect's length in those units, so a 2-bar chase and a 60 s sign border move at the same speed. Results above the learned extreme are clamped.\nchoice: generic value -> kit step ('default' = leave as is). If a choice step sets a numeric key already set by a scale/rate parameter, only its sign is applied (Spirals Movement).\nassume: values xLights doesn't store (e.g. defaults it omits, or a field that saved blank) - {\"KEY\": {\"default\": x, \"extreme\": y}}.\nOverride any of this in seqtool-prefs/xlights.json under param_map. invert: the parameter runs the other way along the learned step (1 = the default end).\nrange [lo,hi]: the value v (0..1) is placed between these absolute values (the kit step only tells which setting it is).\nglides: a parameter given as {\"ramp\": [a, b]} or {\"curve\": [[t, y], ...]} (keyframes, a pin's a..b, a choreography) is written as an xLights value curve on that setting once the kit has learned value curves (0.24.48; a ramp, or a custom curve) - else as a run of short effects stepping from a to b.\ntext: the learned setting is set to the parameter's own text (a face name, a timing track name).",
